ut ‚¤textÙ,But the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ6For such as be blessed of him shall inherit the earth;¦layout ‚¤textÙ0And they that be cursed of him shall be cut off.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter%«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0The steps of a good man are ordered by the LORD:¦layout ‚¤text½And he delighteth in his way.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down:¦layout ‚¤textÙ)For the LORD upholdeth him with his hand.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"I have been young, and now am old;¦layout ‚¤textÙGYet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!He is ever merciful, and lendeth;¦layout ‚¤text¸And his seed is blessed.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter%«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¾Depart from evil, and do good;¦layout ‚¤text·And dwell for evermore.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤text½For the LORD loveth judgment,¦layout ‚¤textÙ:And forsaketh not his saints; they are preserved for ever:¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ,But the seed of the wicked shall be cut off.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%The righteous shall inherit the land,¦layout ‚¤text»And dwell therein for ever.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter%«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+The mouth of the righteous speaketh wisdom,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#And his tongue talketh of judgment.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#The law of his God is in his heart;¦layout ‚¤text¾None of his steps shall slide.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter%«first_verse ªlast_verse"¦verses“„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"The wicked watcheth the righteous,¦layout ‚¤text¸And seeketh to slay him.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(The LORD will not leave him in his hand,¦layout ‚¤textÙ"Nor condemn him when he is judged.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙPWait on the LORD, and keep his way, and he shall exalt thee to inherit the land:¦layout ‚¤textÙ/When the wicked are cut off, thou shalt see it.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse"…¤book§chapter%«first_verse#ªlast_verse$¦verses’„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ&I have seen the wicked in great power,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And spreading himself like a green bay tree.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(Yet he passed away, and, lo, he was not:¦layout ‚¤textÙ-Yea, I sought him, but he could not be found.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse$…¤book§chapter%«first_verse%ªlast_verse&¦verses’„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-Mark the perfect man, and behold the upright:¦layout ‚¤textÙ!For the end of that man is peace.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2But the transgressors shall be destroyed together:¦layout ‚¤textÙ'The end of the wicked shall be cut off.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse&…¤book§chapter%«first_verse'ªlast_verse(¦verses’„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2But the salvation of the righteous is of the LORD:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,He is their strength in the time of trouble.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/And the LORD shall help them, and deliver them:¦layout ‚¤textÙPHe shall deliver them from the wicked, and save them, because they trust in him.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse(